{
  "id": "gary",
  "kind": "character",
  "originStory": "get-what-you-deserve-book",
  "authority": {
    "lockedBy": "gary",
    "lockedOn": "2026-07-16"
  },
  "structured": {
    "sheets": {
      "master": "reference/gary/master.png"
    },
    "requiredForRender": [
      "master"
    ],
    "invariants": [
      "east-asian-man",
      "clean-shaven-no-mustache",
      "double-eyelid-crease",
      "black-hair",
      "light-wash-denim-jacket",
      "claude-mascot-patch-right-chest",
      "yellow-smiley-patch-left-chest",
      "white-crew-neck-tee",
      "white-high-top-sneakers",
      "no-necklace",
      "jacket-back-completely-PLAIN-denim-no-patches-no-artwork-no-text",
      "appears-EXACTLY-ONCE-per-scene-no-other-figure-shares-his-face-hair-or-denim-jacket",
      "religious-iconography-only-where-the-story-calls-for-it-never-decorative",
      "warm-editorial-register"
    ]
  },
  "prose": {
    "voice": "The everyman-teacher and guide: warm, earnest, capable. The human who shows founders how to wield agents. He is the one helping Maya in the book.",
    "lore": "Gary's avatar in this universe, forked from the 'get what you deserve' book's Jerry (the Gary-figure who helps Maya). The narrator-protagonist of the wiki's thesis: the person on the human side who teaches others to command the Chief of Agents.",
    "rules": "Identity of record is reference/gary/master.png (the book's editorial-front likeness with the necklace removed per Gary, 2026-07-16). Pass it as the identity anchor on every render. Signatures: light-wash denim jacket; the orange Claude mascot patch on the RIGHT chest; the yellow smiley patch on the LEFT chest; plain white crew-neck tee; blue jeans; white high-top sneakers. Clean-shaven (NO mustache), clear inked double-eyelid crease at every scale, NO lenses. NO necklace or pendant (removed for this universe). The book's Nation-of-Fire religious signatures (North Star Cross pendant / upper-back cross) are NOT carried here; more broadly, NO religious iconography appears on Gary anywhere in this universe (Gary 2026-07-16: this universe does not promote his faith). BACK TREATMENT, decided by Gary 2026-07-16: the back of the denim jacket is completely PLAIN light-wash denim with NOTHING on it, no patches, no artwork, no text; when a render puts his patches on the back to keep them visible, that is a defect to re-roll, and every from-behind scene prompt should say the back is plain. A real person, but rendered via his established illustrated avatar, not a photo stack; a photo-based realPerson dossier can be added later if photo-accurate renders are ever wanted. SINGLE-INSTANCE RULE (Gary 2026-07-16, from the on-ramps clone defect): Gary appears EXACTLY ONCE per scene. Because his master is passed as a reference, the model tends to bleed his likeness into bystanders; every crowd scene prompt must make the other people visibly distinct (different ethnicities, hair, clothing, explicitly no denim jacket) and a render with a second Gary-like figure is a defect to re-roll.",
    "canonNote": "Churches are NOT banned from this universe (Gary, 2026-07-23). The blanket no-religious-iconography rule was too broad and actively wrong for the work: a core story here is making children's picture books FOR churches, so churches, steeples, and congregations are legitimate story content. What the rule was really guarding against is decorative religious symbolism used as set dressing. That narrower rule is what it now says. Found when a composition asked for churches, the render correctly produced steeples, and the invariant flagged the story rather than the art.",
    "renderRules": "GARY AVATAR LAW: he ALWAYS wears the light-wash denim jacket, and it ALWAYS carries BOTH patches, clearly visible whenever the jacket is in frame: a YELLOW SMILEY-FACE patch on his LEFT chest and the ORANGE CLAUDE MASCOT patch on his RIGHT chest. A bare denim jacket with no patches is a defect, including in dim or night scenes where the patches must still read. Under the jacket a plain WHITE crew-neck tee. He is an east-asian man, CLEAN-SHAVEN with no mustache or beard."
  }
}

